<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cai Shu Du</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a> · Also known as Shu Du of Cai, Cai Shu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cai Shu Du was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-wen-of-zhou">King Wen of Zhou</a> and brother of King Wu, who gave him the fief of Cai in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a>. After King Wu's death he joined the rebellion of the Three Guards against the regency of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-zhou">Duke of Zhou</a>. The revolt was crushed and he was banished, but his son was later restored to Cai, founding its ruling house.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cai-shu-du.jpg" alt="Cai Shu Du" width="320" height="456" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 孫家鼐 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%AC%BD%E5%AE%9A%E6%9B%B8%E7%B6%93%E5%9C%96%E8%AA%AA_%E9%83%AD%E9%84%B0%E5%9B%9A%E8%94%A1%E5%9C%96.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
